  "Question": "What is \\[(-1)^1 + (-1)^2 + \\cdots + (-1)^{2006}?\\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-2006\\)",
    "B": "\\(-1\\)",
    "C": "\\(0\\)",
    "D": "\\(1\\)",
    "E": "\\(2006\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "An odd power of \\(-1\\) is \\(-1\\), and an even power is \\(1\\). Pair each odd-indexed term with the following even-indexed term. Every pair sums to\n\\[\n(-1)+1=0.\n\\]\nBecause \\(2006=2\\cdot1003\\), all the terms fit into \\(1003\\) such pairs with none left over. The sum is \\(\\boxed{0}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
